xnu 0114: publish the display mode and an accelerator stub

With 0112 backboardd enters _detectDisplays and then sits there: QuartzCore
asks the registry for IOAcceleratorES before it looks for a renderer at all,
and this port publishes no such service, so the probe polls for it for 30 s
per process. Even past that point CoreAnimation would draw nothing, because a
display has to carry TimingElements and ColorElements to have a mode at all.

Publish one 60 Hz timing at the panel size and one 8-bit RGB colour mode, and
an empty IOAcceleratorES. It carries neither MetalPluginName nor
MetalPluginClassName, so Metal and OpenGL ES pass it over and CoreAnimation
falls back to its own software rasterizer, which is the renderer this port
has. GetID answers 1 instead of 0, GetBlock 0x40 returns the current mode's
IDs, and selector 77 returns mach_absolute_time().

